  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Rural Afghanistan 2 - Food Security and Natural Resource Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The goal of Empowering Rural Afghanistan 2 is the empowerment of rural communities by working to reduce poverty and improve resiliency in the face of multiple security, political, social, economic, and environmental threats. ERA II builds on the achievements of the ERA I and IRD programs. 

Agriculture development - strenghtening of rural communities so that they are resilient to impacts of natural disasters and climate change and have increased food security and sustainable livelihoods. Agricultural products and methods used in the project are environementally friendly and reduce emissions. Planned activities continue to focus on reducing poverty (SDG1) and inequalities (SDG10) by improving access to  food security (SDG2) and natural resource management (SDG6, 11, 13 and 15), and gender equality and women&#x2019;s empowerment (SDG5).</narrative>
  </description>
